{
  "_comment": "Copy to .mcp.json (gitignored). 'todoist': official hosted MCP, HTTP + OAuth; no token is stored here, sign-in happens in the browser on first tool use. Do NOT also run `claude mcp add todoist ...` if this file exists, duplicate entries cause OAuth sign-in loops. 'ha': the local ha-mcp HTTP server (vendor/ha-mcp, installed by scripts/setup_wsl.sh, run by systemd/assistant-ha-mcp.service); it binds loopback only (127.0.0.1:8086) and the Home Assistant token lives in ~/.config/scherbring-assistant/.env, not here. 'monarch': the vendored community Monarch server (installed by scripts/setup_wsl.sh); its login is a one-time terminal step, see README.md. Scheduled tasks need no MCP entry: scripts/scheduler_dispatch.py runs them from a systemd timer.",
  "mcpServers": {
    "todoist": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://ai.todoist.net/mcp"
    },
    "ha": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8086/mcp"
    },
    "monarch": {
      "command": "./vendor/monarch-mcp-server/.venv/bin/monarch-mcp-server"
    }
  }
}
